ow if we if we nail  it uh and during that 17 days a lot of  things are going to crash right like  just because we are we're going over the  internet we're talking to apis that we  don't control those things spew out 500s  for no good reason or you know if you're  lucky they speed out a 500 if you're  unlucky they just sort of don't answer  your connection and  you know leave it open and never return  a response  so let's start we'd already sort of you  know decomposed our sync engine into  logical steps right more for reporting  and analytics and telemetry but starting  to treat those steps as units of failure  as hierarchical units of failure and you  know sort of if part of the hierarchy  fails you just checkpoint and retry from  there and then figuring out there's some  subtlety to which kinds of retries are  safe and which are not um but most of  them you know most of the time we're  dealing with item operations that are  safe to retry and we can sort of  checkpoint and move on so we put a big  you know investment right around two  years ago uh when census was first  starting to see it's really like you  know higher scale customers into  building out a reasonable recoverable  sync engine that could just sort of pick  up from any failure and keep pressing on  um and that's been a really important  part of our sort of tech stack is like  yeah again the insight there is like if  you get an error basically crash right  and like let your supervisor decide what  to do don't try to handle errors for the  most part  got it well that's your version of  failing gracefully and um you know that  makes a lot of sense  yeah  um so tell us about i mean to the extent  that you're that you're open to sharing  um what are some other features in your  roadmap that you're particularly excited  about like what's coming down the pipe  for census yeah i think um a lot of what  you know now that customers have been  using census you know some of our oldest  customers have been says this in  production for almost three years now um  and a lot of them have been on it for  you know a year or two they're starting  to do richer things they're starting to  do multiple destinations and bring  different teams into it um so there's a  lot of things around like how do we how  do teams collaborate with incenses that  we're excited about i don't know if i  can talk about any specific features yet  but you know how  if you have a data engineering team  that's providing models and you have  a sales operations team that's you know  consuming that for crm and then a cs  team that's consuming that to power you  know their zendesk or whatever their  their cs tool or customer success tool  might be um how can those teams all work  together on the same data um  is an interesting area for us to to kind  of pursue because we are a place um i  think good software tools do this where  different teams come together to  collaborate right like they have a  shared set of you know nouns and verbs  they can talk about together um so  that's one area i'm excited about is  like what we can do to help make  collaboration better with consensus and  help sort of uh you know one of the  things that uh i'm not sure if this is  shipped yet or not but if it hasn't it  will ship very soon like the idea for a  data team to sort of bless a particular  model is saying this is ready for  production this is ready to be synced  versus this one is a draft simple stuff  but like workflowy things that um make  collaboration a lot easier and more  explicit than implicit um so that's  that's one exciting area and then i  think the the bigger picture that we're  sort of tackling this year is you know  we  the data space has been like it's a lot  of early adopters which is great um who  are like you know they know a lot about  their stack they know a lot about you  know their data down to the rows of  columns and they know a lot about the  fields and the semantics of the  destinations and so if you know what you  want to do with data and you know how to  do it census is a great tool for you if  you know what you want to do with data  but you're not exactly sure how to do it  right now we you know we use our sales  engineering our customer data architects  to help you do that but like moving some  more of that into the product is  something we need to do as well is like  i want to follow a pql motion i want to  follow a you know customer support you  know ticket scoring experience like um i  know what data i have i know more or  less in a flowchart sense like how i  want this to work out but i might not  know the details of how that interacts  with the zendesk api you know even  though we sort of abstract that from you  like you're still seeing the artifacts  of that in the census tool so i think  giving people a higher level abstraction  in a way that you know people who are  systems thinkers who are sharp and like  they get it and they know exactly what  they want to happen they just don't like  they don't live and breathe sass apis  a more accessible version of the census  tool um is a really important thing for  us this year is  great  well brad um you know it's been great  chatting with you um we're pretty much  out of time but i did want to ask you a  last question before we let you go and  that's essentially  what surprised you most about your work  in the data ecosystem so far  um  it really is a community more than i  would have guessed right like it's it  really interesting to me to the extent  to which and like a ton of props to the  team at dbt for like building their  their slack and their community because  i think they've headed this um but  there's a lot of other great communities  as well but like the you know the extent  to which people are willing to share  best practices to collaborate to sort of  jump in and help with someone else's  problem that might not even work at your  company just for sort of like you know  the  the the kudos the karma whatever it is  of like you know giving back um is  really heartening um it's like you know  clearly this is a group of people who  sees the world in a different way than  we saw before and they want to spread  that mantra um and that the fact that we  get to be a small part of that is  humbling and pretty awesome um  and yeah i think it's really cool how  you know so much of our sales has been  you know even for a small company like  you know organic through those through  those channels right like where someone  will say well i'm using census to do  this and someone else will say what's  census what's operational analytics  what's reverse ctl um and that starts a  conversation um and that's you know i  think a lot of credit also too to our  team for like really making our first  cohort of customers incredibly happy and  making them all promoters um that's you  know  this is not new startup advice but again  like if you are a founder or you're  going to be a founder right like there  is nothing you could do more than to  make those incredible those first  customers incredibly happy and  incredibly like you know promoters of  your tool um like a thousand people have  said it before but i'll say it again um  and so that like the degree to which  things move through communities in in  the modern data stack and in this world  um  is it not something i would have  expected i thought we'd be doing a lot  more of having you know  we have done some awesome marketing and  i'm really proud of our team for doing  that but i thought we'd be having to do  a lot more of  preaching the gospel ourselves and then  you realize the extent to which our  customers and our partners be preaching  possible for us  yeah that's that's awesome well um we're  excited to have  census be part of data council austin  which is coming up and  to join the data community there um so  we're extremely excited about the irl  event coming up and it will be great to  have you guys participate and folks can  um you know wait and chat with you there  or i'm sure there's other  more digital ways that they can reach  out to you what's the best way for  someone to to get in contact if they  want to learn more about census or  maybe even ask for your advice on on  their data startup  totally um let's see so a few ways you  can like um  best ways to reach me probably are  twitter um so i'm at bradley buddha um  if you sort of like less you know you  know you want help with a startup or an  idea or like hey what is this modern  data stack thing what is this  operational linux thing like help me  understand that i'm happy to like you  know answer questions there um and then  like a shout out to our own community  the operational analytics community if  you go to getcensus.com you can find uh  i should know this but it's one of the  pages i think it's right there on the  homepage to join the operational  analytics community and we have a really  active slack there that's you know  obviously around you know centered  around operational analytics but has a  lot of cool side conversations there as  well um that's a great place to jump in  to learn more about the product um if  you're not yet you know  what maybe you're maybe you're looking  to buy census or a tool like it and you  want to understand how they work or  maybe you just want to learn how this  world works and how you can sort of get  involved in it that's a great place to  come as well so those two my twitter and  operational analytics community  great excellent yeah thank you for  sharing those i'm sure folks will um  find you there  cool well thanks brad um it's been great  to chat with you i hope to see you in  person soon yeah i hope to see you as  well pete and thanks for um you know  taking this time with me and we're  excited to be part of data council and  here coming up soon yeah excellent  and to the rest of our listeners um  thanks for joining us uh next week we'll  have uh another interesting episode of  dc thursday with sumitab mitra from  rudder stack  another important player in the space so  don't forget to  hit your youtube notification bell so  that you get notifications about the  next event  you can find all of our previous dc  thursday episodes also on youtube  in a convenient playlist which we'll  post in the chat  and otherwise we're looking forward to  seeing you all in person soon  thanks again for joining us and and  we'll see you next time
 

